#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161600 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac80eed8-d801-5275-9bd1-73ba43fadb38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "162ebeba-e9ee-5588-8d79-659754a77548" :question/math-academy-id "e-10044" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find the marginal mass function for $X.$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.3}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.7}$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, the marginal mass function for $X$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161806 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "da693f0e-db20-5a7f-9737-3f26d5d6581c" :question/math-academy-id "e-9189" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find $P(X = 0).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{12}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{12}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\dfrac{7}{12}}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{12}$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $\\dfrac{5}{12}$ | $\\dfrac{7}{12}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0) & ={f}_{X}(0) \\\\  & =f(0,0)+f(0,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161807 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "e99dc081-a5d6-5770-a0ea-da172b0d37f5" :question/math-academy-id "e-9190" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(X \\geq 2).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.25}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.5}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.25}$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.35$ | $0.65$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $X$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ | $0.25$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(X\\in {2,3}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =0.5+0.25 \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "302ba10f-6301-5406-a6eb-a791023086bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388696} {:answer/id #uuid "921de448-3d22-5cd1-a54f-e39044c7efe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388697} {:answer/id #uuid "e6333532-a3fd-5b53-b5cd-7f3df872c4ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388698} {:answer/id #uuid "a287a941-39cf-5d42-b3ad-215fe829e3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388699} {:answer/id #uuid "8bac6d53-e8d5-532a-b489-fe067c6a0e3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "921de448-3d22-5cd1-a54f-e39044c7efe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388697} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad0cee9-7157-5677-948e-794efe862f54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8031fb9a-8406-5da3-9e4c-34e027c59fc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-142552" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find $P(Y=2).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=2) & ={f}_{Y}(2) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(1,2) \\\\  & =0.4+0.3 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d46262e-4406-55da-93ce-fcf75006cc0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388703} {:answer/id #uuid "97d79ff2-57ad-553d-ae4f-3f2c9c395f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388704} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf00ace-9c33-5b2e-98a5-6a3e61f07580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388705} {:answer/id #uuid "0a5356c5-5162-5e45-a56a-53460085ebe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388706} {:answer/id #uuid "9141c099-038d-51b2-aab3-6314285529cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbf00ace-9c33-5b2e-98a5-6a3e61f07580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388705} :answer-field/id #uuid "802dd67f-c7f4-50a7-9efa-5ea7e2d940d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0249a8c-1fbb-5835-b939-3578d912e959" :question/math-academy-id "q-142557" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find ${f}_{Y}(2).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.35$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(2) & =f(0,2)+f(1,2) \\\\  & =0.2+0.05 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ff31d70-3b48-523c-977a-4700ae71b603" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388710} {:answer/id #uuid "2e6bcb1f-7037-5424-8495-568442e3dd70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388711} {:answer/id #uuid "1a070c7d-f0cc-5b67-be85-2e2e0e166551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388712} {:answer/id #uuid "82b2922d-2b78-5a4e-ba18-3d059fb47d30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388713} {:answer/id #uuid "d8af2b71-db11-56b0-9d6f-becf80793ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82b2922d-2b78-5a4e-ba18-3d059fb47d30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388713} :answer-field/id #uuid "7445110f-ddd2-5f85-8896-ee365bf08aef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ee01b22e-38eb-5520-85b6-65e91b69b278" :question/math-academy-id "q-142559" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find $P(Y=1).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=1) & ={f}_{Y}(1) \\\\  & =f(1,1)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07d5acd4-e203-58d4-90f2-c07ee9108231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388717} {:answer/id #uuid "edb504d6-b7af-5844-b244-23334aa6a89b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388718} {:answer/id #uuid "dbb20272-08b5-5d2f-a9c8-c017418e94a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388719} {:answer/id #uuid "896a41b4-0ee9-59a2-88f5-e36f384641e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388720} {:answer/id #uuid "de7a07cb-d37e-502f-9218-217589772148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbb20272-08b5-5d2f-a9c8-c017418e94a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388719} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac33a33-87e3-5df3-9af9-1bef7215740d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97819980-67b8-5b84-b61a-6542f5deacd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-142561" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find ${f}_{X}(3).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.1+0.15 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "980c2c9b-f4cc-5079-bc60-ce6ed2fa1532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388724} {:answer/id #uuid "84f82dce-5870-555c-81cd-6e3b0d4733dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388725} {:answer/id #uuid "43d251e7-9972-53ee-8e41-95b3b4b55300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388726} {:answer/id #uuid "9c25a75b-20d2-5306-a98c-16e5c4d461c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388727} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf82a49-e517-502c-9d81-1ff57e2e8dbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c25a75b-20d2-5306-a98c-16e5c4d461c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388727} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf06d9e2-0e07-5e82-80c0-a1b15f9d80b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b26e44a-bf92-58fd-9171-7d593acbfbdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-142562" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find $P(Y=2).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=2) & ={f}_{Y}(2) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(2,2)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.25+0.05+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "276c5ae6-df9d-5f8e-9807-2e0d616e5f11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388731} {:answer/id #uuid "d8deb50e-79b6-56a9-ac5d-47c4501b81ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388732} {:answer/id #uuid "48deacc9-2775-5153-beaa-0f9bfc574a4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388733} {:answer/id #uuid "561f4d55-6954-53f7-b0ec-98d22fb329c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388734} {:answer/id #uuid "ae15abf1-e86a-5111-b4c9-da11bd1a9069" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8deb50e-79b6-56a9-ac5d-47c4501b81ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388732} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4b06fa8-953d-5e68-94fe-9d9930d8ac21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8fa0761f-0e18-5863-ae2f-db25cb746dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-142572" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.35$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(X<2).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.35$ | $0.1$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $X$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.45$ | $0.2$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & =P(X\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=1) \\\\  & =0.35+0.45 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "779d02b1-0285-5656-a5c8-4ab14dfe8ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388738} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e57118-95ef-5cf1-abe2-d2aa68db8b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388739} {:answer/id #uuid "f337b0f9-9449-54fb-ae90-b1f1dcb7a200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388740} {:answer/id #uuid "061fc762-4753-5e4c-8e7b-519586e8cce2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388741} {:answer/id #uuid "1c112452-64cc-5f49-bf43-64119ab92d09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c112452-64cc-5f49-bf43-64119ab92d09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388742} :answer-field/id #uuid "753c1c0a-517c-59ee-8f5b-d8ffba8e56bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "504c6adf-0647-5414-8b4c-090d7ea47b26" :question/math-academy-id "q-142575" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(Y<2).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{4}{7}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $\\frac{5}{7}$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $Y$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{5}{7}$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<2) & =P(Y\\in {1}) \\\\  & =P(Y=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "835217a4-d6a2-5dd5-8659-84135a515386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388745} {:answer/id #uuid "2864b101-6085-52d5-8378-6eadcf8d3b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388746} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad6495c-8275-51de-ae3f-cc887b29b2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388747} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d458ad-38f6-5650-8ab7-4209de6e0e3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388748} {:answer/id #uuid "6d09c576-0bf0-5c4b-9e30-f7aa829ec996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d09c576-0bf0-5c4b-9e30-f7aa829ec996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388749} :answer-field/id #uuid "5958cea9-8fca-5086-acaf-2a49747a1e80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70d19739-3637-5291-b9d5-a437e0e2cbed" :question/math-academy-id "q-142714" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(Y\\le 1).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $Y$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le 1) & =P(Y\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =P(Y=0)+P(Y=1) \\\\  & =0.25+0.3 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7d571aa-54e3-5759-ace3-f24cd16bc673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388752} {:answer/id #uuid "97aecea0-a36d-54e2-8eee-0e837887b041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388753} {:answer/id #uuid "baf84851-495f-5c91-bc72-1eea31f3c289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388754} {:answer/id #uuid "fb7efe77-b797-5937-bd53-c7290168dca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388755} {:answer/id #uuid "79f25296-1781-5f7f-9f15-87fab5e1f98e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb7efe77-b797-5937-bd53-c7290168dca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388755} :answer-field/id #uuid "12d342d1-92cb-5e54-b57b-4ba693b2bea6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9c560696-9fe2-5c0b-8c1e-d2fdd8325ece" :question/math-academy-id "q-142718" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(|Y|>0).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $Y$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.45$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|Y|>0) & =P(Y\\in {-1,1}) \\\\  & =P(Y=-1)+P(Y=1) \\\\  & =0.2+0.45 \\\\  & =0.65.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5057c784-3b6f-5be3-a773-8136d4487223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388759} {:answer/id #uuid "a211a1ba-5eab-5511-a5f7-83c8049b7abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388760} {:answer/id #uuid "be35ec8f-6f49-5031-a2dd-753140dfd835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388761} {:answer/id #uuid "a9df6888-4d6f-559c-8fae-2cf03535fa00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388762} {:answer/id #uuid "1816b1fd-2ffd-504b-be07-9315a6d28211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9df6888-4d6f-559c-8fae-2cf03535fa00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388762} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cfdad6f-4dae-58fb-b1f6-c89ffa9aa643" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "71472c4f-96c7-5ae0-a350-14b4fab5ebd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-142723" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(Y\\ge 1).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $Y$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\ge 1) & =P(Y\\in {1,2}) \\\\  & =P(Y=1)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =0.2+0.25 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388764 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac80eed8-d801-5275-9bd1-73ba43fadb38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1d324da-f52a-52e5-919f-70e421f3c7b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388766} {:answer/id #uuid "69833fb5-a91c-5779-9079-552ef129b2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.45$ | $0.55$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388767} {:answer/id #uuid "4f73bd53-c145-5435-a5fc-3172230ea80f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388768} {:answer/id #uuid "294395cf-8362-56a8-9eac-de51672ac335" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.75$ | $0.25$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388769} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d03416-7617-5400-8c14-b65551a0e576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69833fb5-a91c-5779-9079-552ef129b2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.45$ | $0.55$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388767} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac932547-8894-54b2-bd1b-5de19e20a0a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 