$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{12}{25}$ | $\\frac{13}{25}$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388790} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f78820e-4400-5026-a48d-c0476f6c2233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "958dfdfa-a17e-58dd-bc47-e06cde22da21" :question/math-academy-id "q-142834" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{3}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{25}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{4}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find the marginal mass function for $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{3}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{25}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{4}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{14}{25}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{6}{25}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $\\frac{12}{25}$ | $\\frac{13}{25}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, the marginal mass function for $Y$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{12}{25}$ | $\\frac{13}{25}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/